       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The current FDA label for amlodipine lists a maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. I don't know of any labeled indication or revision that allows 50 mg. I can't check the label from here, but this contradicts what I know of it. A single 50 mg dose could cause profound hypotension and shock, and the effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg daily.** Tell me which one and I'll enter it now.\n- **Check the label.** If you have a source for 50 mg, please look again at the dosing section. I'd be glad to reconsider if it says something different.\n- **Ask pharmacy.** If you think there's a special reason for this dose, a pharmacist or the attending can review it and enter it directly.\n\nIf the goal is stronger blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide is the usual approach. That's your call, and I can enter those orders if you want."
      }
